1
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:43,500
Ever wonder what your life would be like with
different parents? A boy named North did.

2
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:21,000
North is a comedy, family, fantasy film directed by Rob Reiner.

3
00:10:52,500 --> 00:10:58,500
Eleven-year-old North has had it with his parents.

4
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:36,000
They are always busy with their careers and don't give North the
attention he needs, so he files a lawsuit against them.

5
00:18:07,500 --> 00:18:13,500
The judge rules that North should either find new parents or
return to his own parents within two months.

6
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:51,000
Thus North starts off on a journey around the world to
find parents that really care about him.

7
00:25:22,500 --> 00:25:28,500
North, played by Elijah Wood.

8
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:06,000
Narrator (voice), played by Bruce Willis.

9
00:32:37,500 --> 00:32:43,500
North's Dad, played by Jason Alexander.

10
00:36:15,000 --> 00:36:21,000
North's Mom, played by Julia Louis-Dreyfus.

11
00:39:52,500 --> 00:39:58,500
Arthur Belt, played by Jon Lovitz.

12
00:43:30,000 --> 00:43:36,000
Judge Buckle, played by Alan Arkin.

13
00:47:07,500 --> 00:47:13,500
North is a 1994 American comedy-drama adventure film directed by Rob Reiner.

14
00:50:45,000 --> 00:50:51,000
The story is based on the 1984 novel North: The Tale of a 11-Year-Old Boy Who Becomes a Free Agent and Travels the World in
Search of the Perfect Parents by Alan Zweibel, who co-wrote the screenplay and has a minor role in the film.

15
00:54:22,500 --> 00:54:28,500
The cast includes Elijah Wood in the title role, with Jon Lovitz, Jason Alexander, Alan Arkin, Dan Aykroyd, Kathy
Bates, Faith Ford, Graham Greene, Julia Louis-Dreyfus, Reba McEntire, John Ritter, and Abe Vigoda.

16
00:58:00,000 --> 00:58:06,000
Bruce Willis narrates and plays several different roles throughout the film, and a
9-year-old Scarlett Johansson appears briefly in her film debut.

17
01:01:37,500 --> 01:01:43,500
This was the final theatrical film for Alexander
Godunov before his death the following year.

18
01:05:15,000 --> 01:05:21,000
The film was shot in Hawaii, Alaska, California,
South Dakota, New Jersey, and New York.

19
01:08:52,500 --> 01:08:58,500
It was produced by Castle Rock Entertainment and New Line Cinema
and released by Columbia Pictures on July 22, 1994.

20
01:12:30,000 --> 01:12:36,000
North was a box office bomb, grossing $12 million
against its $40 million budget.

21
01:16:07,500 --> 01:16:13,500
North was panned by critics, and has been referred to
as one of the worst films ever made.

22
01:19:45,000 --> 01:19:51,000
The film explores themes of parent child relationship, child
prodigy, young boy, travel, based on children's book.

23
01:23:22,500 --> 01:23:28,500
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
